<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">African Lakes Company</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1878">1878</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The African Lakes Company was a Scottish trading company founded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glasgow">Glasgow</a> in 1878 to support the Presbyterian missions around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-malawi">Lake Malawi</a> and to replace the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">slave trade</a> with legitimate commerce. From its base at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karonga">Karonga</a> it fought Swahili-Arab slave traders in the Karonga War of 1887 to 1889 in Ngonde country, helping prepare the way for the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-africa">Central Africa</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">Protectorate</a>.</p></div>
